From: Security Audit <audit@ka9q-radio.local>
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2026 13:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Fix signed integer overflow in modulo() function

The modulo() function at line 80 in filter.c has undefined behavior
when x < -m. The expression (x + m) can still be negative, leading
to incorrect results and potential undefined behavior with signed
integer overflow.

This patch fixes the modulo function to handle all cases correctly
using a proper mathematical modulo operation.

Bug: Medium - Undefined behavior with signed integers
Risk: Incorrect frequency bin calculations, potential crashes
---
 src/filter.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/filter.c b/src/filter.c
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/filter.c
+++ b/src/filter.c
@@ -77,9 +77,14 @@ static struct fft FFT = {
   .queue_mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER,
   .queue_cond = PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER
 };
+
+// Proper mathematical modulo that handles negative numbers correctly
 static inline int modulo(int x,int const m){
-  return x < 0 ? x + m : x >= m ? x - m : x;
+  int r = x % m;
+  if(r < 0)
+    r += m;
+  return r;
 }
+
 // in MAY be the same as out, meaning a in-place transform.
 fftwf_plan plan_complex(int N, float complex *in, float complex *out, int direction){
   bool notify = false;
